{"challenges":[{"attack":"Could “current instruction” be asserted absolutely despite the possibility of a later, unsupplied change?","claim_id":"current-supported-time","outcome":"survives","result":"The claim is expressly limited to “Among the supplied records.” Within that two-record set, [schedule-amendment:109-148 \"This amendment replaces the time in v1.\"] makes the v2 time controlling; it does not establish that no later record exists.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Could the replacement statement be too vague to identify which record or field it changes?","claim_id":"replacement-statement","outcome":"survives","result":"The statement specifically names both the operation and target: [schedule-amendment:109-148 \"This amendment replaces the time in v1.\"].","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Could the v2 time be inferred from chronology alone rather than stated in the amendment?","claim_id":"amended-time","outcome":"survives","result":"The time is directly stated in [schedule-amendment:79-108 \"Thursday at 10:00 local time.\"]. The Tuesday creation label is unnecessary to the conclusion.","tool_ids":[]},{"attack":"Could the original time be confused with the replacement time?","claim_id":"original-time","outcome":"survives","result":"The original record directly states [schedule-original:51-80 \"Thursday at 09:30 local time.\"], while the amendment separately supplies the replacement time.","tool_ids":[]}],"checks":[{"basis_reasoning":"This is a mechanically valid attribution to the supplied original record: [schedule-original:0-17 \"Draft schedule v1\"] and [schedule-original:51-80 \"Thursday at 09:30 local time.\"]. Source attribution alone does not establish real-world truth beyond the supplied record.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"original-time","reasoning":"The claim accurately reports what the supplied v1 text says. Its external_fact basis is appropriate for a source assertion.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"This is a mechanically valid attribution to the supplied amendment: [schedule-amendment:0-19 \"Signed amendment v2\"] and [schedule-amendment:79-108 \"Thursday at 10:00 local time.\"]. It establishes source content, not independently verified scheduling reality.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"amended-time","reasoning":"The claim accurately reports the stated v2 time. The source-assertion basis is appropriate.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"The cited supplied text exactly states [schedule-amendment:109-148 \"This amendment replaces the time in v1.\"]. This supports attribution of that sentence, rather than an independent proof of its authority outside the supplied records.","basis_verdict":"source_attributed","checked_step_ids":[],"claim_id":"replacement-statement","reasoning":"The claim is an accurate report of the amendment's express replacement language.","verdict":"supported"},{"basis_reasoning":"The derivation is supported by proof steps read-original-time, read-amendment, and apply-replacement. The first supplies the v1 time, the second supplies the v2 time and replacement relation, and the third applies that explicit relation only within the supplied two-record set. No named external theorem is required.","basis_verdict":"applicable","checked_step_ids":["read-original-time","read-amendment","apply-replacement"],"claim_id":"current-supported-time","reasoning":"The central conclusion follows from the stated times and explicit replacement relation. Its wording appropriately limits “current” to the supplied records and preserves that 09:30 is the original v1 entry.","verdict":"supported"}],"missing_evidence":["No evidence rules out a later amendment or other unsupplied instruction superseding v2.","The supplied records do not identify the locality or time-zone identifier meant by “local time.”"],"recommended_action":"finish","tool_requests":[]}
